# graphify Knowledge Graph

`graphify-out/graph.json` is the project's navigable knowledge graph. Prefer it over grep for architecture and relationship questions.

## Before answering codebase questions

1. Check that `graphify-out/graph.json` exists.
2. Run `graphify query "<question>"` first.
3. Use `graphify path "<A>" "<B>"` or `graphify explain "<concept>"` when tracing dependencies.
4. Fall back to `GRAPH_REPORT.md` or source files only if the graph lacks enough context.

Do not invent relationships not present in graph output.

## After modifying code

Run `graphify update .` (AST-only, no API cost) before answering questions about the changed area.

If `graphify-out/needs_update` exists after doc/markdown changes, semantic re-extraction is stale — run `graphify update .` and mention that docs may need a full `--update` pass.

## Local graph artifacts

`graphify-out/` is gitignored and stays local — not pushed to GitHub. Each developer rebuilds with `graphify update .` after pulling code changes.

## Background automation

- `post-commit` hook rebuilds the graph for code changes (log: `~/.cache/graphify-rebuild.log`)
- `post-checkout` hook rebuilds on branch switch
- Brand logo SVGs under `apps/web/public/media/` are excluded from semantic extraction — low information value
